@	
s	accounts	Prints the list of accounts
s	check	Check whatever you need
s	clean	Clears the cache and deletes all artifacts
s	compile	Compiles the entire project, building all artifacts
s	console	Opens a hardhat console
s	flatten	Flattens and prints contracts and their dependencies
s	help	Prints this message
s	node	Starts a JSON-RPC server on top of Hardhat Network
s	run	Runs a user-defined script after compiling the project
s	test	Runs mocha tests
o	config	A Hardhat config file	
o	--emoji	Use emoji in messages	
o	--max-memory	The maximum amount of memory that Hardhat can use	
o	--help	Shows the help text or task's help if name is provided	V
o	--network	The network to connect to	
o	---show-stack-traces	Show stack traces	
o	--verbose	Enables Hardhat verbose logging	
o	--version	Shows hardhat's version	
@	accounts
@	check
@	clean
o	--global	Clear the global cache	
@	compile
o	--force	Force compilation ignoring cache	
o	--quiet	Makes the compilation process less verbose	
@	console
o	--no-compile	Don't compile before running this task	
@	flatten
@	help
@	node
o	--fork	The URL of the JSON-RPC server to fork from	
o	--fork-block-number	The block number to fork from	
o	--hostname	The host to which to bind to for new connections	
o	--port	The port on which to listen for new connections (default: 8545)	
@	run
o	--no-compile	Don't compile before running this task	
@	test
o	--no-compile	Don't compile before running this task	
